nded by Wikivoyage"],["Greenwich Heritage and Meridian Tours","activity",51.48271,-0.00861,"","","","","","r","Operated by the Greenwich Tour Guides Association, the original guiding organisation that has operated in Greenwich for 25 years. Walking tours take place twice a day (every day, excluding 24-26 Dec, 1 Jan and London Marathon Day). No…"],["Greenwich Royal Tours","activity",51.48314,-0.00869,"","","","","","r","Runs a range of more in-depth tours including Greenwich Day Tour, Greenwich Highlights Half Day Tour, Greenwich Food Tour and National Maritime Museum Tour. Tickets must be booked in advance and tours leave from outside the Greenwich…"],["Trinity Laban Conservatoire of Music and Dance","activity",51.48,-0.01,"","","","","","r","An internationally renowned school for music and dance training based in the Old Royal Naval College and a contemporary site by Deptford Creek. Put on musical and dance performances across Greenwich throughout the year - many of them free."],["St. Alfege Church","activity",51.4805,-0.0097,"Greenwich Church St, SE10 9BJ","","","","","r","A beautiful Baroque church designed by Nicholas Hawksmoor (and is rumoured to have links with Occultists, Freemasons and such-like). Hosts classical music concerts and organ recitals. Its Christmas choir is enjoyable also."],["Up The Creek Comedy Club","activity",51.48184,-0.01152,"302 Creek Rd, SE10 9SW","","","","","r","Comedy club. Hosts hilarious stand-up as well as music nights."],["Greenwich Tall Ships Festival","activity",51.48396,-0.01069,"","","","","","r","Annual festival held at the start of July. Tall sailing ships cruise down the Thames from Woolwich, with Greenwich town centre being a fantastic place to view them. Each evening of the festival concludes with a spectacular fireworks…"],["NG1 Golf","activity",51.49913,-0.00051,"265 Tunnel Ave, SE10 0QE","Mon-Sat 8AM-11PM; Sun 8AM-9PM","","","","r","Urban driving range against the spectacular backdrop of Canary Wharf. Restaurant and bar on site. 18 years + age policy after 6PM."],["Walk the Thames Path","activity",51.48329,-0.01082,"","","","","","r","Greenwich is home to the last 4 miles (6.4 km) of the 184-mile-long Thames Path, organised by National Trails. From Cutty Sark, the path follows the river up and around the Greenwich Peninsula before ending at the Thames Barrier. The…"],["The Kings Arms","restaurant",51.48091,-0.00796,"16 King William Walk","","","","","r","This pub is well situated for the tourist attractions in Greenwich and does good bar food."],["The Mogul Tandoori","restaurant",51.4812,-0.00938,"10 Greenwich Church St","","","","","r","This restaurant provides excellent Nepalese and Northern Indian cuisine in an unusual and interesting setting (as long as you get seated downstairs, below street level)."],["Tai Won Mein noodle houses","restaurant",51.481,-0.00916,"","","","","","r","Offers budget Chinese cuisine, at a budget price if you're after a bargain rather than quality. They only take cash. Noodle Time and Saigon are located around the street, facing each other, and offer similar fare/price."],["Old Brewery","restaurant",51.4817,-0.01032,"Pepys Building","Daily 10AM-11PM","","","","r","Part of the local Meantime Brewery's growing empire with a massive enclosed outdoor area - great in the summer months. Part of the same building as the tourist information centre, and perhaps more popular with tourists than locals…"],["Greenwich Market Food Court","restaurant",51.48158,-0.00908,"Greenwich Market, SE10 9HZ","Sat and Sun","","","","r","Expanded in 2016, Greenwich Market's outdoor food court is now a dedicated section of the market. Dozens of street food stalls offer a range of cuisines from around the world. Seating is limited, so it is best to buy your food and eat…"],["Buenos Aires Cafe","restaurant",51.48084,-0.00895,"15 Nelson Rd, SE10 9JB","Mon-Thu 10AM-10PM; Fri Sun 9AM-10PM","","","","r","Casual Argentinian cafe with steaks, Spanish-themed food and brunch. Relaxing orangery and garden at the rear."],["Spanish Galleon","bar",51.48167,-0.00992,"48 Greenwich Church St, SE10 9BL","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Tsar Peter the Great Monument","sight",51.4834,-0.0191,"Deptford Creek","","","","","r","Tsar Peter the Great Monument, which is located at the waterfront adjacent to Deptford Creek and paid for by the Russian government to commemorate the cultural exchange between two great seafaring nations (it could be argued that…"]]}